# CI before main

A subagent does not push and does not merge. The parent says that in the launch prompt. The parent is the only one that pushes, and only after the checks below pass.

Do not push to `main` unless the user explicitly asked to push or merge there. Do not force-push `main`. Land on a pull request. Cloud Agents already work on their own branch and open a pull request. Do not tell one to push `main`.

Before the push or merge, run the checks that match the files changed. Stop if any fail.

The same split is what `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs. Path rules live in `scripts/ci/classify_changes.py`.

- `backend/` or `scripts/qa/check_workspace_deps.py`: from `backend/`, `uv lock --check`, `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run mypy packages/ apps/`, and `uv run pytest --tb=short`. From the repo root, `uv run --no-project python scripts/qa/check_workspace_deps.py`.
- `apps/`, `packages/`, `package.json`, or `package-lock.json`: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build`.
- `apps/web/`, `packages/ui/`, or `packages/api-client/`: also `npm run e2e --workspace=apps/web`.
- `labs/raw-context-brain/`: in that directory, `npm ci`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm test`.
- A safety path (c10, the safety-gate app, `evals/safety/`, `docs/safety/`, or the two audience rule files): from `evals/safety`, `uv run --project ../../backend pytest tests/ -v --tb=short`.
- `db/**` or `infra/local/Dockerfile.postgres`: do not merge until the DB migrations check on the pull request has passed.
- `docs/` or `scripts/check-capability-index.py`: `python3 scripts/check-capability-index.py`.

A green pull request does not deploy a cluster. A push to `main` runs the verify jobs again. When that push changes a deploy input (backend, web, packages, db, helm other than the image-updater write-back, or `infra/k8s/`), CI also runs the kind smoke: deploy plus `npm run e2e:smoke`, not the full browser suite. A commit that only touches `infra/helm/wellbe-local/.argocd-source-wellbe.yaml` does not start CI. Build images still publishes changed images.

After a merge to `main`, watch CI and Build images. If either fails, say so and fix it before the next change.
